   "claims": [
    "To calculate its volume, you need to multiply the base area (area of a circle: π × r²) by height and by 1/3: volume = (1/3) × π × r² × h A cone with a polygonal base is called a pyramid – see pyramid volume calculator.",
    "The calculator now displays the volume of the cone – in our case, it's 37.7 cu in.",
    "Apply the cone volume formula: volume = (1/3) × a × h if you know the base area, or volume = (1/3) × π × r² × h otherwise.",
    "Recall that the cone volume formula reads: volume = (1/3) × π × r² × h So in our case, we have the following: volume = (1/3) × π × 1² × 3 So the volume of our cone is exactly π!",
    "As we all know, this can be approximated as volume ≈ 3.14159."
   ],
